  "confounders": [
    "a co-deleted neighbour is indistinguishable from the gene that carries the effect; loss_genes_that_are_the_same_event lists the pairs this sweep cannot separate",
    "a loss enriched in one lineage brings that lineage's dependencies with it; no lineage covariate is fitted here, so a hit can be a lineage effect wearing a gene's name",
    "significance is not effect size: with about a thousand lines a shift of 0.05 gene-effect units reaches p = 0.015, so every row carries the two group medians beside the p-value",
    "a damaging-mutation call is a prediction about a variant's consequence, not a measured absence of protein, and a heterozygous damaging mutation is counted as loss"
  ],
